# Smoke test of the runner (not a spec): with the caret inside the text, what goes in goes in there, ⌫ the app has takes
# the character before the caret, and the text before the caret reads the same where the field tells it (a field that
# tells nothing of its text has nothing to read, so it isn't among the profiles).
NAME     text goes in at a caret inside the text, and the text before it reads the same
PROFILES nstextview chromium electron
LANG     chinese
TEXT     "Hi |Bob"
TYPE     nihao
KEY      space
EXPECT   doc "Hi 你好|Bob"
EXPECT   context before "Hi 你好"
KEY      backspace
EXPECT   doc "Hi 你|Bob"
EXPECT   context before "Hi 你"
EXPECT   nolost
EXPECT   calls length<=1
